---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import site from '../../site.config.mjs';
import { url } from '../lib';
const analyticsEnabled =
  site.analyticsId !== 'G-XXXXXXXXXX' && /^G-[A-Z0-9]+$/.test(site.analyticsId);
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Encrypted Cat Games"
  description="How the Encrypted Cat Games website and The Cradle: Episode 01 on iPhone and iPad handle your information."
>
  <article class="container article legal">
    <header class="article-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Your privacy.</h1>
      <p>Website and app privacy policy · Updated October 15, 2026</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This policy describes how Encrypted Cat Games (Encrypted Cat / 0xKOT)
        handles information through this website and in The Cradle: Episode 01
        for iPhone and iPad. For privacy questions or requests, contact{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers the studio website, contact pages, website analytics,
        and links used here, and the iPhone and iPad version of The Cradle:
        Episode 01. Games running on itch.io are also subject to itch.io’s
        privacy policy and the game’s own data practices.
      </p>
      {!site.nativePrivacyConfirmed && (
        <div class="notice">
          <strong>Native game releases</strong>
          <p>
            Privacy disclosures for future iPhone and iPad releases will be
            added here before those releases. The website policy does not yet
            describe native game data collection.
          </p>
        </div>
      )}
      {site.nativePrivacyConfirmed && (
        <section id="the-cradle-episode-01-ios" aria-labelledby="ios-heading">
          <h2 id="ios-heading">The Cradle: Episode 01 on iPhone and iPad</h2>
          <p>
            This section covers the App Store version of The Cradle: Episode 01.
            The game works fully without sending anything about you. There is no
            account, no advertising, and no tracking: the app does not use the
            advertising identifier (IDFA) and does not track you across other
            companies’ apps or websites, so it never asks for tracking
            permission.
          </p>
          <h3>Anonymous statistics (only if you say Yes)</h3>
          <p>
            On the title screen the game asks once whether to send anonymous
            play statistics. Nothing is sent until you choose Yes; No, or not
            answering, means nothing is sent. With a Yes, the game sends short
            events such as a session starting, a checkpoint or ending reached,
            an achievement unlocked, and a frame-rate range, together with the
            game’s version, language, graphics settings, and the operating
            system family. A random session number is kept in memory only and is
            new every session. Your name, email, anything you type, your saves,
            contacts, photos, microphone, camera, precise location, and device
            identifiers are never collected. You can change your answer at any
            time in Settings → Interface → Anonymous statistics.
          </p>
          <p>
            The statistics are processed for us by{' '}
            <a href="https://aptabase.com">Aptabase</a>, a privacy-focused
            analytics service, and stored in its United States region. Aptabase
            uses your connection’s IP address only to work out the country and
            region and to count daily users with a hash whose salt changes every
            24 hours; it does not store IP addresses. Aptabase keeps analytics
            data for up to 5 years. See{' '}
            <a href="https://aptabase.com/legal/privacy">
              Aptabase’s privacy policy
            </a>
            . The legal basis is your consent, which you can withdraw in the
            settings at any time. Because the statistics contain nothing that
            identifies you, we cannot find, show, or delete one player’s data.
          </p>
          <p>
            In the App Store’s privacy details, this is declared as Coarse
            Location, Product Interaction, and Performance Data: not linked to
            you, used for analytics only, and not used for tracking.
          </p>
          <h3>Saves and settings</h3>
          <p>
            Your progress, settings, achievements, and personal bests stay on
            your device. The app keeps them in its own web storage, with a spare
            copy among the app’s own files, which iOS includes when it backs up
            the app. They are never sent to us. Deleting the app removes them
            from the device; “Reset progress” in the game clears both copies.
          </p>
          <h3>Game Center</h3>
          <p>
            Game Center is optional; you can play without signing in. It is
            Apple’s service, and Apple’s privacy policy applies to it. The game
            only reports achievement progress to Game Center, and reads back
            achievements you have already unlocked.
          </p>
          <h3>Purchase, links, and permissions</h3>
          <p>
            The game is a paid app sold and delivered by Apple through the App
            Store. Apple handles payment, and Apple’s privacy policy covers the
            purchase and download; we receive no payment information. Apart from
            the opt-in statistics, the app reaches no internet service. Links in
            the game (Discord, Reddit, and the credits) open in Safari, where
            those sites’ own policies apply. The game never uses your microphone
            and never records sound.
          </p>
          <h3>Children</h3>
          <p>
            The Cradle is a horror game and is not directed at children under
            13. We do not knowingly collect information from children, or
            personal information from anyone.
          </p>
        </section>
      )}
      <h2>gobnative browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        The gobnative player reads installers and game files you select locally.
        It stores imported games, saves, settings, and any optional HD packs in
        this browser’s IndexedDB storage. These files are not uploaded to us.
        Clearing this website’s data removes that local storage; browsers may
        also clear it automatically. Website analytics do not read these files.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact and support messages</h2>
      <p>
        If you contact us, we receive the email address, message, game
        selection, topic, and any information you choose to share. We use this
        information to reply, troubleshoot issues, and manage the enquiry.
        Please do not send passwords, payment information, or sensitive personal
        data.
      </p>
      {site.formEndpoint ? (
        <p>
          The contact form uses Formspree to process submissions and forward
          them to our support inbox. Formspree may process technical information
          for delivery and spam prevention. See{' '}
          <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">
            Formspree’s privacy policy
          </a>
          . Our inbox is provided by Gmail.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          The contact form currently prepares an email draft locally and opens
          your email app, with a fallback link if it does not open. The website
          does not upload your draft. Sending it from your email app delivers it
          to our Gmail inbox under your email provider’s practices.
        </p>
      )}
      <p>
        We keep enquiry information while it is needed to respond and follow up.
        You can request deletion by contacting us; some information may need to
        be retained to meet legal obligations.
      </p>
      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This static website is hosted through GitHub Pages. GitHub may process
        connection information, including IP addresses, for security and service
        operation. See{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
          GitHub’s privacy statement
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        {analyticsEnabled
          ? 'Google Analytics loads only if you choose Allow in the analytics prompt. If you decline, or make no choice, it does not load and no analytics cookies are set. You can change your choice at any time with Cookie settings in the footer.'
          : 'Google Analytics is currently disabled. The website contains a placeholder configuration that does not load Google Analytics.'}
      </p>
      <p>
        When enabled, Google Analytics measures page visits and usage, including
        browser and device information. It may store analytics cookies.
        Advertising features are disabled in our configuration, and contact form
        contents are not sent as analytics events. See{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">
          Google’s privacy policy
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <h2>Third-party content and links</h2>
      <p>
        Game links open itch.io in a new tab. We do not embed itch.io widgets or
        load its content on this website. When you visit itch.io, its own data
        practices apply under{' '}
        <a href="https://itch.io/docs/legal/privacy-policy">
          itch.io’s privacy policy
        </a>
        . Devlog images are hosted with this site. Video links and community
        links open external services; their own privacy policies apply when you
        visit them.
      </p>
      <h2>Local storage and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        If you allow analytics, Google Analytics stores first-party cookies to
        measure visits. Your analytics choice is saved in your browser’s local
        storage so we don’t ask again; choosing Decline in Cookie settings
        removes the analytics cookies. This website does not use an account
        system. Your browser settings let you block or clear cookies and locally
        stored preferences.
      </p>
      <h2>Your requests</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask about information you have sent us, request correction or
        deletion, or raise a privacy concern by emailing{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Depending on where
        you live, you may have additional rights under applicable privacy law.
      </p>
      <h2>Policy updates</h2>
      <p>
        We will update this page when website services or game data practices
        change, with a new date at the top. Any future native release will be
        added here, by name, before it reaches the App Store.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="text-link" href={url('contact/')}>
          Contact Encrypted Cat Games
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
